A||||0||ezsurf||Cam Install Tip
Z||000000||ezsurf||05-31-99||08:44 PM||||<br>I finally got my engine back from the machine shop.  The block had to be bored .030 over, but the crankshaft was good.  Although I am still assembling it, this is a good tip for anyone changing a cam.  Install the cover plate on the back side of the cam shaft first.  Then, turn the block vertically with the flywheel side down.  Insert the cam vertically into the block.  This is 100 times easier than trying to install it horizontally.  Also, immediately put on the timing chain/gears and the front cover.  This will prevent the cam from sliding out when you turn it back horizontal.  I hope I didn't nick a cam bearing.  I'm still doing cosmetic work, but I going to try to get the engine back in next weekend.
